  "question": {
    "text": "A triangle <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi><mi>C</mi></math> lying in the first quadrant has two vertices as <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>. If<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8736;</mo><mi>B</mi><mi>A</mi><mi>C</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>90</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi></msup><mo>,</mo></math>and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>ar</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>&#916;</mi><mi>ABC</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn><msqrt><mn>5</mn></msqrt></math>&nbsp;sq. units, then the abscissa of the vertex&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math> is :"
  },
